# Sync user documentation with WebPortal edits

Files under this glob are **user-facing application code** (modules, modals, router, data helpers that drive UI, shell). If your edit changes behaviour, copy, navigation, or routes:

1. Update **`WebPortal/help/index.html`** (contextual topic: summary, steps, screenshot path if needed).
2. Update **`WebPortal/help/user-manual.html`** for the relevant module chapter (and the route appendix if **`appRouteConfig.json`** changed).
3. Run **`node scripts/apply_user_guide_help_links.mjs`** when help anchors or modal titles change.
4. Regenerate user-guide screenshots if the screen layout changed: **`cd e2e && npm run capture-user-guide`**.

Treat documentation updates as **part of the same commit** as the feature fix or feature work, not a follow-up unless explicitly out of scope.

See also the always-on rule **User guide and module manual** in `user-guide-update.mdc`.
